<h1>Andre Vasquez</h1>
<p>40th Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027. Incumbent.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.andrefor40th.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (andrefor40th.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Said in June 2026 that he would seek reelection to the City Council rather than run for mayor, and planned a July 16 kickoff for his bid for a third term. His campaign site presents him as an on-the-ground consensus-builder focused on basic services, funding public schools and community safety, citing his work on the ECPS civilian police oversight ordinance and license plate reader cameras in the ward.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>40th Ward alderman since 2019; co-chair of the City Council Progressive Caucus since 2023; former community organizer with Reclaim Chicago, AT&amp;T account manager and hip-hop artist.</p>
